 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to one entity and has a `name`, a `slug` (unique within the entity), an `is_active` flag (default `true`) and optional `labels_i18n` (per-locale labels). Implemented by `App\Models\Queue`. Plan limits on the number of queues are not enforced yet.
+
 ### Ticket
 
-Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
+Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
 
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
+- Display `code` (see below).
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
-- Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance timestamp `issued_at` (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` or `printed` (`App\Enums\TicketChannel`).
+- Status: `waiting` or `called` (`App\Enums\TicketStatus`). There is no cancelled status.
+
+**Display code.** Per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, … (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; beyond 999 it grows: `A1000`, `A1001`). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`. The next code is the last *valid* code + 1 **by insertion order**, not string order (`A999` then `A1000` → `A1001`). A deleted ticket's number is not reused when a later ticket exists (`A001..A003` with `A002` deleted → next is `A004`). Codes not matching `A<digits>` are skipped (only `A-X` → `A001`; `A001` then `A-X` → `A002`). See `Ticket::nextCode()`.
+
+**Issuance** (`App\Actions\IssueTicket`):
+
+- Rejects inactive queues with `InactiveQueueException`. The queue row is locked and re-read inside the transaction, so a queue deactivated after the caller loaded it is still rejected. Nothing is persisted on rejection.
+- A unique `(queue_id, code)` collision (concurrent issuance) is retried a few times.
+- New tickets are `waiting`, `issued_at = now()`, default channel `virtual`, default priority `0`. A negative priority throws `InvalidArgumentException`.
+
+**Write-once.** After issuance, any Eloquent save/update changing a field other than `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`) throws `LogicException`.
+
+**Single call.** `Ticket::call(User)` marks the ticket `called` and records `called_at` and the calling user. Only members of the ticket's entity may call (otherwise `AuthorizationException`, ticket unchanged). Calling a non-waiting ticket throws `LogicException`; the status is checked against the database under a row lock. Choosing *which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is not implemented yet.
 
